---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Play · Fourth Wall Gaming"
  description="Run your first session — install the Mythras GM plugin for Claude Code, pick a campaign, and open the first scene. With a way to check each step actually worked."
>
  <article class="prose play">

    <header class="masthead">
      <p class="kicker">Mythras GM · Claude Code</p>
      <h1>Run Your First Session</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        Claude as your Gamesmaster, running Mythras Imperative with a real dice engine and every
        wound, faction and journal entry persisted in a knowledge graph. This page takes you from
        nothing to an open scene — <em>and tells you how to check each step actually worked.</em>
      </p>
    </header>

    <h2>Before You Start</h2>
    <p>Three things. Two of them you probably already have.</p>
    <div class="prereqs">
      <div class="card prereq">
        <span class="eyebrow">Required</span>
        <strong class="val">Claude Code</strong>
        <span class="note">The engine ships as a plugin, so everything below is typed at a <a href="https://claude.ai/code">Claude Code</a> prompt.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card prereq">
        <span class="eyebrow">Required</span>
        <strong class="val">uv</strong>
        <span class="note">The CLI runs under <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/">uv</a>. Without it there is no dice tower and no save file.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card prereq">
        <span class="eyebrow">Handled for you</span>
        <strong class="val">TypeDB 3.8</strong>
        <span class="note">Fetched once on first run — about 25&nbsp;MB, self‑contained, no Docker and no JVM.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small">
      Native builds cover macOS and Linux on x86_64 or arm64, and Windows on x86_64. Anywhere else,
      the engine can run its database under Docker instead — see <code>/mythras-gm:setup</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Install, One Step at a Time</h2>
    <p>
      Install the engine explicitly and first. Campaigns declare it as a dependency, but do not
      rely on that resolving for you — when it silently doesn't, the campaign's own diagnostics
      go down with it, and you get a plugin that simply isn't there rather than an error.
    </p>

    <div class="switch" role="group" aria-label="Choose a campaign">
      <span class="switch-label">Campaign</span>
      <button class="pill" type="button" data-camp="purewater" aria-pressed="true">Purewater</button>
      <button class="pill" type="button" data-camp="veilwrack" aria-pressed="false">Veilwrack</button>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps">

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Add the marketplace</h3>
        <p>One source holds the engine and every campaign.</p>
        <div class="cmd">
          <pre id="marketplace"><code>/plugin marketplace add fourth-wall-gaming/mythras-gm</code></pre>
          <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="marketplace">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="confirm">
          <span class="eyebrow">Confirm</span>
          <p>The marketplace lists three plugins: <code>mythras-gm</code>, <code>purewater</code> and <code>veilwrack</code>. If you see fewer, stop here rather than continuing.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Install the engine</h3>
        <p>This is the dice tower, the rules graph and the save file. Nothing else works without it.</p>
        <div class="cmd">
          <pre id="engine"><code>/plugin install mythras-gm@fourth-wall-gaming</code></pre>
          <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="engine">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="confirm">
          <span class="eyebrow">Confirm</span>
          <p><strong>mythras-gm</strong> appears in your installed plugins. Do not move on until it does.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Install a campaign</h3>
        <p>
          Pick one. <span data-camp-prose="purewater">Purewater is a Classic Fantasy port — a canal city, three days before a tournament.</span><span data-camp-prose="veilwrack" hidden>The Veilwrack is an original sky realm — winged peoples on floating bone-spires, and the wind is dying.</span>
          You can install both and keep two saves side by side.
        </p>
        <div class="cmd">
          <pre id="campaign"><code>/plugin install <span data-camp-cmd>purewater</span>@fourth-wall-gaming</code></pre>
          <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="campaign">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="confirm">
          <span class="eyebrow">Confirm</span>
          <p>Both <strong>mythras-gm</strong> and <strong data-camp-name>purewater</strong> are installed. Two plugins, not one.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Start a fresh session and read the first line</h3>
        <p>
          Both plugins check the game at session start, so quit Claude Code and open it again.
          The preflight tells you exactly where you stand — it never imports anything and never
          blocks the session, so whatever it says is safe to act on.
        </p>
        <div class="confirm">
          <span class="eyebrow">Confirm — one of these</span>
          <p><code>…installed but has not been imported into the database yet</code> — expected on a first run. Continue to step&nbsp;5.</p>
          <p><code>the mythras-gm engine is not installed</code> — step&nbsp;2 didn't take. Run it again.</p>
          <p><code>PREFLIGHT FAILED — uv is not installed</code> — install <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/">uv</a>, then start another session.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Open the scenario</h3>
        <p>
          This imports the campaign, briefs you on Mythras if you're new to it, walks you through
          choosing or rolling a character, and opens the first scene. Run it once, ever.
        </p>
        <div class="cmd">
          <pre id="start"><code>/<span data-camp-cmd>purewater</span>:start</code></pre>
          <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="start">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="confirm">
          <span class="eyebrow">Confirm</span>
          <p>You are asked whether you've played Mythras before, and then offered characters. If instead the narration simply begins, something didn't import — see below.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <h3>Every session after that</h3>
        <p>One command, forever. The preflight will have already told you the clock and session number.</p>
        <div class="cmd">
          <pre id="play"><code>/mythras-gm:play</code></pre>
          <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="play">Copy</button>
        </div>
        <div class="confirm">
          <span class="eyebrow">Confirm</span>
          <p><code>a game is in progress</code> — with your campaign's clock and session number. Never run the start command again; it is only for a campaign that has not begun.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

    </ol>

    <h2>Where Your Save Lives</h2>
    <p>
      The files in a campaign plugin are a scenario seed, not a save. The moment you run the start
      command, the database becomes the game — and the database is on disk, at
      <code>~/.claude/mythras-gm/typedb/data</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Where you play</th><th scope="col">What happens to the save</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Your own machine</td>
            <td>Persists indefinitely. Close the laptop, come back in a month, pick up mid-scene.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>A cloud session</td>
            <td>Lives only as long as that session's container. A new session starts with an empty database and no campaign.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="eyebrow">Worth knowing before you invest an evening</span>
      <p>
        If you play in a disposable cloud environment, the campaign does not survive it. You'll be told
        the campaign "has not been imported yet" — which is true, and reads exactly like a fresh
        install rather than a lost one. Play on a machine that keeps its disk, or export the campaign
        to a folder you control before the session ends.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>When Something Is Wrong, It Will Be Quiet About It</h2>
    <p>
      The characteristic failure here is not a crash. It's a database that isn't there, or a schema
      that never loaded, while the game carries on narrating over the top of it. Learn the tells.
    </p>
    <ul class="symptoms">
      <li>Nothing is printed at session start. Both plugins always say something; silence means neither hook ran.</li>
      <li>The GM narrates straight into a scene without offering you a character.</li>
      <li>A wound, a spent luck point or a journal entry from last session has quietly reverted.</li>
      <li>Dice results appear in the prose but no roll is reported.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>One command answers all of them. It checks the install end to end and reports every stage as pass or fail, in order:</p>
    <div class="cmd">
      <pre id="setup"><code>/mythras-gm:setup</code></pre>
      <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="setup">Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="confirm">
      <span class="eyebrow">Confirm</span>
      <p>Every check reads true, ending in <code>Ready.</code> Any check that reads false is named, with the reason attached.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Two Campaigns, and a Word About Spoilers</h2>
    <div class="campaigns">
      <div class="card accent-ruby camp">
        <span class="eyebrow">Classic Fantasy</span>
        <h3>And Then the Dragons Came: Purewater</h3>
        <p>
          A canal city where the Lake Lady's waters meet the sea. Baron Hanzo di Teufel has arrived
          for the Tourney with a champion nobody is allowed to see, and there are three days left
          before it all goes wrong.
        </p>
        <span class="stat">4 entry points · 42 characters · 15 agendas on clocks</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card accent-cobalt camp">
        <span class="eyebrow">Original setting</span>
        <h3>The Veilwrack: The Stilling</h3>
        <p>
          No ground — an endless sky above the toxic Undermist. The winged Alar live on the
          floating bone-spires of dead sky-leviathans, and Lanternfall's windlane began Stilling this
          season. Nobody has said the word aloud yet.
        </p>
        <span class="stat">4 spires · 7 factions · 3 playable Alar</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="eyebrow">If you intend to play rather than run</span>
      <p>
        Don't browse the campaign repositories. They are the published source of the scenario, so
        they hold the Gamesmaster's material — the secrets, the timeline and who everyone
        actually is. Much of it is marked GM-only, but not all of it, and a scenario is easy to spoil
        by accident. Install the plugin and let the game show you. Both worlds are built so that what
        you don't witness happens anyway, which only works if you haven't read ahead.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Love the System? Buy the Books</h2>
    <p>
      This runs on the <em>Mythras Imperative</em> SRD under the ORC License.
      <a href="https://thedesignmechanism.com">The Design Mechanism</a> publishes the full
      <em>Mythras</em> line — get the real thing and play it at a real table too.
    </p>

  </article>

  <div class="toast" id="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite">Copied</div>

  <style>
    /* ---------- masthead ---------- */
    .masthead { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .kicker {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    }
    .masthead h1 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
    .standfirst {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .standfirst em { color: var(--text); }

    .small { font-size: 0.9rem; }

    .eyebrow {
      display: block;
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
    }

    /* ---------- prerequisites ---------- */
    .prereqs {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr));
      margin: 1.25rem 0;
    }
    .prereq { padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.25rem; }
    .prereq .val { font-size: 1.15rem; font-variant: small-caps; letter-spacing: 0.03em; color: var(--text); }
    .prereq .note { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-dim); line-height: 1.5; }

    /* ---------- campaign switch ---------- */
    .switch { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem; }
    .switch-label {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin-right: 0.35rem;
    }
    .pill {
      appearance: none;
      cursor: pointer;
      font: inherit;
      font-variant: small-caps;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 2px;
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      border: 2px solid var(--rule-strong);
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .pill:hover { border-color: var(--ruby); color: var(--ruby); }
    .pill[aria-pressed="true"] {
      background: var(--ruby);
      border-color: #4d130c;
      color: var(--bg-raised);
    }

    /* ---------- steps ---------- */
    .steps {
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: step;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .step {
      counter-increment: step;
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 3.25rem;
    }
    .step::before {
      content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 0.15rem;
      font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: var(--ruby);
    }
    .step h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    }
    .step > p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
    @media (max-width: 30rem) {
      .step { padding-left: 0; padding-top: 1.5rem; }
    }

    /* ---------- command block ---------- */
    .cmd { position: relative; margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }
    .cmd pre { margin: 0; padding-right: 4.5rem; }
    .copy {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0.55rem;
      right: 0.55rem;
      appearance: none;
      cursor: pointer;
      font: inherit;
      font-variant: small-caps;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
      border-radius: 2px;
      background: transparent;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      color: var(--text-dim);
    }
    .copy:hover { border-color: var(--ruby); color: var(--ruby); }

    /* ---------- confirm strip ---------- */
    .confirm {
      margin-top: 0.75rem;
      border-left: 4px solid var(--emerald);
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--emerald) 9%, var(--bg-raised));
      padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem 0.7rem;
      border-radius: 0 2px 2px 0;
    }
    .confirm .eyebrow { color: var(--emerald); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    .confirm p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.5; }
    .confirm p + p { margin-top: 0.4rem; }

    /* ---------- callout ---------- */
    .callout {
      margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
      border-radius: 2px;
      padding: 1rem 1.15rem 1.05rem;
    }
    .callout .eyebrow { color: var(--amber); margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .callout p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }

    /* ---------- table ---------- */
    .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 1rem; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 28rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    th, td {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      vertical-align: top;
      color: var(--text-dim);
    }
    th {
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule-strong);
    }
    td:first-child { font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); white-space: nowrap; }

    /* ---------- symptoms ---------- */
    .symptoms { padding-left: 0; list-style: none; margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem; }
    .symptoms li {
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 1.6rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }
    .symptoms li::before {
      content: '✦';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      color: var(--amber);
    }

    /* ---------- campaign cards ---------- */
    .campaigns {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }
    .camp { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
    .camp h3 { margin: 0.1rem 0 0.25rem; }
    .camp p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .camp .stat {
      margin-top: auto;
      padding-top: 0.75rem;
      font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }

    /* ---------- toast ---------- */
    .toast {
      position: fixed;
      left: 50%;
      bottom: 1.25rem;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      background: var(--text);
      color: var(--bg-raised);
      font-variant: small-caps;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      padding: 0.45rem 1rem;
      border-radius: 2px;
      opacity: 0;
      transition: opacity .18s;
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 20;
    }
    .toast.show { opacity: 1; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .toast { transition: none; } }
  </style>

  <script>
    const pills = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.pill[data-camp]'));

    function select(key: string) {
      pills.forEach((p) => p.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(p.dataset.camp === key)));
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-camp-cmd], [data-camp-name]').forEach((el) => {
        el.textContent = key;
      });
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-camp-prose]').forEach((el) => {
        el.hidden = el.dataset.campProse !== key;
      });
    }

    pills.forEach((p) => p.addEventListener('click', () => select(p.dataset.camp!)));

    const toast = document.getElementById('toast');
    let toastTimer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;
    function flash(msg: string) {
      if (!toast) return;
      toast.textContent = msg;
      toast.classList.add('show');
      clearTimeout(toastTimer);
      toastTimer = setTimeout(() => toast.classList.remove('show'), 1400);
    }

    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy[data-copy]').forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const target = document.getElementById(btn.dataset.copy!);
        if (!target) return;
        const text = target.textContent?.trim() ?? '';
        if (navigator.clipboard?.writeText) {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(
            () => flash('Copied'),
            () => flash('Press ⌘C to copy'),
          );
        } else {
          flash('Press ⌘C to copy');
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</Base>
